# Copy to .env.local (which is gitignored) and fill in. Vite only exposes
# variables prefixed VITE_, and everything exposed ends up in the built bundle.

# CARTO raster basemaps. Without it the CARTO layers are simply omitted, so the
# map still works -- Esri Ocean and Satellite need no key at all.
#
# This key WILL be visible to anyone who opens the site: a client-side basemap
# fetches tiles from the browser, so the key travels in the URL. That is how
# CARTO intends it to work, and it is why the protection is a DOMAIN
# RESTRICTION set on the CARTO dashboard, not secrecy. Restrict it to the
# GitHub Pages origin before the site is public.
#
# Free to 5,000,000 tile requests a month across the whole account.
# CARTO and OpenStreetMap attribution must stay visible: carto.com/attributions
VITE_CARTO_KEY=

# Where the published Zarr archive lives. Defaults to ./data for local work.
# For the Hugging Face dataset:
#   VITE_DATA_BASE=https://huggingface.co/datasets/AdityaRugs/MaritimeSARoperations/resolve/main
VITE_DATA_BASE=
